From cff3722d94678790533aa89f1e5a5837d4dc41af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:24:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0013b-b70-ple-int8-nvme-lookahead

On top of 0013 (INT8 PLE table from NVMe), two knobs, both default to v1:

B70_PLE_INT8_NVME_READER=py|native|uring: native = a C pthread pool that
pread()s a whole batch in one ctypes call (GIL released); uring = one
io_uring per reader via raw syscalls (liburing is not in the image), QD =
B70_PLE_INT8_NVME_IO_THREADS. Built from embedded C source with gcc at first
use (B70_PLE_INT8_NVME_NATIVE_DIR / _NATIVE_LIB). Failed or short native
reads go through the v1 retry path.

B70_PLE_INT8_NVME_LOOKAHEAD=1 (design 3.3): after step k's gather launch the
model state predicts every prefilling request's next chunk
(plan_next_chunks), D2H-copies its tokens from req_states.all_token_ids
before the hook's sync, and a per-rank background thread hashes them, skips
cached rows and reads the rest with its own store into job-owned buffers.
Step k+1's hook takes the job (waits if it predicted this step, cancels
otherwise), resolves its lookups first (hits protected), serves misses from
the prefetched rows before any sync read, then installs unused prefetched
rows best effort. The cache keeps a single writer (the step thread);
correctness never depends on the lookahead. The stats line reports rows
served from the lookahead and hook waits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
